			"notes": "## Highlights\n\n- Added dedicated **Forge 26.2** and **NeoForge 26.2** builds.\n- Split the former 26.x artifacts into explicit 26.1.x and 26.2.x JARs so incompatible Minecraft generations cannot load the wrong file.\n- Expanded same-JAR compatibility across supported Minecraft patch releases, from Forge 1.18 through 1.21.11, NeoForge 1.21 through 1.21.11, and Forge/NeoForge 26.1 through 26.2.\n\n## Compatibility fixes\n\n- Added a Forge 1.20.6 runtime compatibility layer for changed mappings and server APIs.\n- Supported both Forge 1.21 EventBus generations and late-patch API changes.\n- Preserved `/matrix` command permissions across NeoForge 1.21 patch releases.\n- Corrected legacy Forge logging, parent-event forwarding, and minimum loader declarations.\n- Fixed affected Forge servers remaining alive after shutdown because of NightConfig watcher threads.\n\n## Matrix and bridge reliability\n\n- Reused Matrix transaction IDs during retries to prevent duplicate messages after timeouts.\n- Added bounded Matrix connection and request timeouts.\n- Fixed bridge bootstrap, reload, and shutdown races that could leave background threads running or throw null-state errors.\n- Improved temporary event-tap expiration handling.\n\n## Event Tap fixes\n\n- Fixed listener and `EventIndex` leaks after repeated `/matrix reload` operations.\n- Reused event indexes between reloads instead of repeatedly scanning the full classpath.\n- Added clear diagnostics and retry behavior when event indexing fails.\n- Fixed event indexing when the server path contains spaces or non-ASCII characters, including NeoForge `union:` JAR paths.\n- Prevented event lookup from triggering arbitrary class static initialization.\n- Cached hot-path reflection lookups and removed unused per-tick reflection.\n\n## Packaging and validation\n\n- The release now contains nine server-only JARs: Forge 1.18.x, 1.19.x, 1.20.x, 1.21.x, 26.1.x, and 26.2.x; plus NeoForge 1.21.x, 26.1.x, and 26.2.x.\n- Release metadata now synchronizes Minecraft versions, loader, Java, and Server tags across Modrinth and CurseForge.\n- The same release JARs passed packaged server tests and real Synapse end-to-end tests across 45 runnable Minecraft/loader combinations.\n\n## Upgrade notes\n\n- No configuration or saved Matrix sync-state migration is required.\n- Use Java 17 for Forge 1.18–1.20, Java 21 for Forge/NeoForge 1.21.x, and Java 25 for Forge/NeoForge 26.1–26.2.\n- Minecraft 26.1 and 26.2 require their respective version-specific JARs.\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/ControlNet/minecraft-matrix-bridge/compare/v0.1.4...v0.1.5"
		},
